      "wms_title" "National Oceanographic Data Centres"
      "wms_abstract" "This map shows the locations of National Oceanographic Data Centres (NODCs) within the International Oceanographic Data and Information Exchange (IODE) network. This information is intended to help users find the relevant data centre. NODCs are institutions officially designated by IOC Member States to provide access to and stewardship of national oceanographic data resources. They receive data from research, monitoring and operational programmes, apply quality-control procedures and agreed standards, preserve the data and the information needed to interpret it, and make national ocean data available for science, services, assessments and decision-making. They support data management planning, exchange data internationally and contribute to products such as statistical summaries and ocean atlases."
